            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0109" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/667: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-22T11:00:00+01:00">May 22, 1940—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—8:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Department’s 55, May 21. American citizens with valid passports able to
                    proceed promptly to Genoa from Switzerland to return to the United States. No
                    Swiss exit visas or Italian entrance and exit visas required for American
                    citizens. Through car rail connections between Zurich and Genoa re-established
                    yesterday via Saint Gotthard. Convenient connections also between Bern, Geneva,
                    Lausanne and <pb facs="0110" n="101" xml:id="pg101"/> Genoa via Simplon with
                    single change at Milan. Duration of journey Bern Genoa 9½ hours.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
